        <mxCell id="2fHWJIsyqpY3oujbUqMn-733" connectable="0" parent="2fHWJIsyqpY3oujbUqMn-732" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];fontFamily=Times New Roman;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(166, 128, 184);&quot;&gt;[fault present] &lt;b&gt;fault treatment&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" x="0.4932" y="-1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="18" y="11" as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2fHWJIsyqpY3oujbUqMn-734" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;fontColor=#000000;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=none;fillStyle=solid;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;gradientColor=#FFF2A1;shadow=1;size=0;pointerEvents=1;align=left;fontFamily=Times New Roman;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;120&quot; data-end=&quot;170&quot; style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Hanmer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;says&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p data-svelte-h=&quot;svelte-j66wve&quot;&gt;The failure lifecycle consists of four phases:&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p data-start=&quot;283&quot; data-end=&quot;412&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;116&quot; data-end=&quot;135&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;Error Detection&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt; – Detect deviation from expected behavior.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Complete Parameter Checking, Reasonableness Check, Acceptance Test, Time-out, Heartbeat / Watchdog&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;283&quot; data-end=&quot;301&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;Error Recovery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt; – Restore correct state after an error occurs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Retry, Rollback, Rollforward, Restart, Checkpoint / Restore&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;414&quot; data-end=&quot;434&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;Error Mitigation -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Limit impact while the error persists -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Compensation, Graceful Degradation, Redundancy, Diversity, Voting&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;566&quot; data-end=&quot;585&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;Fault Treatment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt; – Address or remove the root cause of the fault&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Reconfiguration, Isolation, Replacement, Reinitialization, Escalation&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="470" x="-2300" y="6690" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2fHWJIsyqpY3oujbUqMn-735" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;fontColor=#000000;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=none;fillStyle=solid;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;gradientColor=#FFF2A1;shadow=1;size=0;pointerEvents=1;align=left;fontFamily=Times New Roman;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;By explicitly managing constituent join, leave, and role changes at the SoS lifecycle level, we reduce the disturbance frequency and duration seen by the service layer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As reliability maturity increases (Levels 2–3), structural coordination and reconfiguration absorb instability earlier, reducing the complexity required from service-level fault tolerance mechanisms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In higher levels, fewer and simpler compensation mechanisms are needed because reliability is partially ensured at the SoS coordination level rather than solely within the CEP service.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="470" x="-1430" y="6670" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2fHWJIsyqpY3oujbUqMn-1094" edge="1" parent="1" source="2fHWJIsyqpY3oujbUqMn-1098" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontFamily=Times New Roman;" target="2fHWJIsyqpY3oujbUqMn-1124">
